      "text": "## The Measure-Theoretic Foundation"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#012",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:probability-statistics:00-overview, git-history:probability-statistics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "probability-statistics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "probability-statistics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:probability-statistics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "probability-statistics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "probability-statistics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Probability and Statistics - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Before 1933 (Kolmogorov's axiomatization), probability was informal. Kolmogorov grounded it in measure theory — the same framework used for Lebesgue integration."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#013",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:probability-statistics:00-overview, git-history:probability-statistics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "probability-statistics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "probability-statistics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:probability-statistics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "probability-statistics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "probability-statistics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Probability and Statistics - Landscape Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  MEASURE THEORY                    PROBABILITY THEORY\n  (from analysis)                   (Kolmogorov)\n  +-----------------------+         +-----------------------+\n  | Measurable space      |  maps   | Probability space     |\n  | (Omega, F)            | ------> | (Omega, F, P)         |\n  |                       |   to    |                       |\n  | Measure mu: F->[0,inf)|         | Measure P: F -> [0,1] |\n  | (total mass arbitrary)|         | (total mass = 1)      |\n  +-----------------------+         +-----------------------+\n           |                                  |\n           v                                  v\n  Measurable function               Random variable\n  f: Omega -> R                     X: Omega -> R  (same thing)\n           |                                  |\n           v                                  v\n  Integral f dmu (Lebesgue)         E[X] = Integral X dP\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#014",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:probability-statistics:00-overview, git-history:probability-statistics:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "probability-statistics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "probability-statistics/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:probability-statistics:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
